{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqax0ldtaim","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"headless permission allowlist for nightly QA shell calls","summary":"Nightly QA runs stalled because the headless auto-mode classifier cannot statically verify command substitution $(), for/while loops, heredocs, env-var prefixes (VAR=x cmd), or cd-prefixed compounds — those Bash calls prompt and the 2am run dies (Jun 12 run: first date call waited 2.1h, a $()-for-loop killed it). Fix pattern: (a) minimal reviewable allowlist in zonoid/.claude/settings.json — Bash(npm test), Bash(./scripts/qa-suite.sh *), Bash(date -u *), plus the 8 orchestrator-graph MCP tools the QA skill uses; (b) committed arg-validated wrapper scripts/qa-suite.sh replaces ad-hoc node/loop sweeps (the script is the trust boundary — never allowlist bare interpreters); (c) SKILL.md now has a Headless shell discipline section; foreign test_cmd not covered by the allowlist ⇒ skipped, never improvised. Read-only basics (grep, tail, jq, cat, ls, sed -n) are auto-approved and need no entries.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-12T12:41:07.649Z","vec":null,"actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-12T12:41:07.654Z"}
